# Mintlify documentation (Student Label System)

## Project layout

- MDX pages live in `docs/` with YAML frontmatter (`title`, `description`)
- Site config: `docs/docs.json` (not mint.json)
- Preview: `npm run docs:dev` from repo root

## Terminology

- **Label ID** — barcode/QR identifier (e.g. `1979-JJ-0000001`)
- **Student ID** — demographic ID for reporting
- **BE** — Basic Education; **ESL** — English as a Second Language
- **Data Lead**, **Data Member**, **Intake Member** — capitalize role names
- **Cabinet / drawer** — physical file storage; **archive box** — end-of-year storage unit

## Writing style

- Active voice, second person ("you")
- Sentence case for headings
- Bold UI labels: Click **Admin → Cabinets**
- Link to live app paths when helpful: `https://student-label-system.vercel.app/intake`

## Mintlify components

Prefer Mintlify components over raw HTML:

- `<Steps>` / `<Step>` for workflows
- `<CardGroup>` / `<Card>` for overview links
- `<Note>`, `<Tip>`, `<Warning>` for callouts
- Tables for role/permission matrices

Use the **mintlify-platform** MCP to look up component syntax. Use the **mintlify** Admin MCP to create or edit pages and navigation.

## MCP URLs

| Server | URL |
| --- | --- |
| Admin (write) | `https://mcp.mintlify.com` |
| Platform docs | `https://mintlify.com/docs/mcp` |
| Published site (after deploy) | `https://YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.mintlify.app/mcp` |

After adding a page, update `docs/docs.json` navigation if it is a new top-level route.
